  "title": "Nearchus's voyage from the Indus to the Persian Gulf",
  "summary": "In autumn 325 BCE Nearchus took Alexander the Great's fleet from the Indus delta west along the barren coast of Makran, losing three ships to a storm. He met Alexander at Harmozeia and then sailed on along the Persian Gulf, reaching Susa by February 324 BCE according to the sources opened.",
